# Daisy Plan Workflow

When `PLAN.md` exists at the workspace root, it is an active Daisy implementation plan. The file lives in `.daisy/plans/` (symlinked from the Daisy home) and is gitignored.

**In Cursor Plan mode:**
- Collaborate on `PLAN.md` only — do not write implementation code.
- Fill in: Goal, Non-goals, Constraints, Steps (as `- [ ]` checkboxes), Risks, Test Plan, Deferred, Open Questions (numbered list).
- End every response with the Open Questions list and: "Ready to execute? (yes/no)"

**In Cursor Agent mode (executing a plan):**
- Read `PLAN.md` before starting; set `**Status:** executing`.
- Re-read `$DAISY_ROOT/prompts/praxis.md` before each step (the Steps section will remind you).
- Work through steps in order; mark each `- [x]` on completion.
- After each step: update Decisions if you deviated; move anything out of scope to Deferred.
- Stop and report on blockers — do not skip or work around them silently.
- When all steps are complete: append ` *Built*` to the H1 title; set `**Status:** built`.

**To archive a completed plan:**
Run `daisy plan-archive` or say `/daisy archive PLAN.md`.
This moves the plan file to `.daisy/plans/archive/` and removes the `PLAN.md` symlink.
